# Form Creation Rules

## Stack

- **Zod** — Schema validation for form values and API request/response.
- **React Hook Form** — Form state, `useForm`, `FormProvider`; use `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with `zodResolver(schema)`.
- **Toast** — Use toast (e.g. shadcn Sonner) to show success or error messages after form submit.

## Reusable Form Fields

- **Common fields** (text, textarea, number, select, **upload**, etc.) → implement as reusable components under `@/components/forms/`.
- Use shadcn `Form`, `FormField`, `FormItem`, `FormLabel`, `FormControl`, `FormDescription`, `FormMessage` and wire a single primitive (e.g. `Input`, `Textarea`, file input) plus optional `description`.
- Prefer existing: `FormFieldText`, `FormFieldTextarea`, `FormFieldUpload`, etc. Add new ones (e.g. `FormFieldSelect`) when a pattern repeats.
- **Form-specific or one-off fields** (e.g. highly custom file UI with unique layout or non-standard behavior) → keep inline in the form component; do not force into a generic wrapper.

### Example (reusable text field)

```tsx
<FormFieldText
  control={form.control}
  name="displayName"
  label="Display name"
  placeholder="Your name"
  description="Optional helper text"
/>
```

### Example (reusable upload field)

```tsx
<FormFieldUpload
  control={form.control}
  name="avatar"
  label="Avatar"
  uploadType="avatar"
  accept="image/*"
  description="PNG, JPG or WebP. Max 2MB."
/>
```

## Form Logic Location:
- Location `@lib/{name}`
- Form submit endpoint using API routes with `create-api-handler`

## Toast feedback

- After form submit via API: show **success** with `toast.success("...")` or **error** with `toast.error("...")` (or equivalent, e.g. `toast("...", { variant: "destructive" })`).
- Use the message from the API when available (e.g. `res.error` or `res.message`); otherwise use a sensible default.

### Example (in onSubmit / after fetch)

```ts
const res = await fetch("/api/...", { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify(values) });
const data = await res.json();
if (res.ok) toast.success(data.message ?? "Saved.");
else toast.error(data.error ?? data.message ?? "Something went wrong.");
```